#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064218 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064090 :question/id #uuid "48ec6930-88b7-5aad-9bb7-c5e23e766f80" :question/math-academy-id "e-470" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{9}{4\\sqrt{1-9x^2}} \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^2}}\\textrm{d}u = \\arcsin(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u^2$ as the variable, we have $9x^2 = (3x)^2.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=3x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 3 \\,\\textrm d u=\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe can now write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{9}{4\\sqrt{1-9{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{9}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(3x)^{2}}}\\,\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{12}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡3x+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de1e3f3a-5a64-573f-8fb1-9952fa36a839" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050628 :topic/difficulty 0.8280730284227736 :topic/id #uuid "5a0d0fb8-c0a3-55dc-a497-9f0d5f0eda76" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064203} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064204} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064205}] :topic/math-academy-id 334 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048557} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050101}] :topic/title "Integrating Algebraic Functions Using Substitution"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050675 :topic/difficulty 0.9247314504586539 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428831 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected acc