{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/9}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/3)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)}^{2}.$  \n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{3}.$ Differentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=3\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/3)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (3\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290599 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "107a9f41-2502-55f7-8a6a-ad9668d4d961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(9x)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288156} {:answer/id #uuid "26fda1ba-8631-59b5-be99-a0b25adfb1b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288289} {:answer/id #uuid "3dd4480a-eb47-5df7-8f7d-7d8a0364fcf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288453} {:answer/id #uuid "d611d7c2-8a82-5a2a-819e-f3aaaf3c8caf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}{(9x)}^{2}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289454} {:answer/id #uuid "fe0ca68c-3ad4-59cd-a28c-b4af3a7ea2b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(3x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3dd4480a-eb47-5df7-8f7d-7d8a0364fcf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288453} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc6db447-0452-575d-91d0-4892a31cf97a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290140}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "125b10d6-12e0-5b91-bec6-9d12798feef7" :question/math-academy-id "q-2506" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-9{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $9{x}^{2}=(3x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=3x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-9{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(3x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(3x)}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329722 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e102532-1da6-505c-8449-9cc76869ce8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327613} {:answer/id #uuid "7a1a0201-5d52-55b8-abe6-b78bfe3139ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327981} {:answer/id #uuid "c31eb764-054a-5f59-8e49-ecb141552eb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328639} {:answer/id #uuid "df2c1966-1b2a-5a6d-bb6c-45c4f8885c1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{arcsin}\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328889} {:answer/id #uuid "e319cc83-daa7-5ab6-89e3-973218f6e0a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c31eb764-054a-5f59-8e49-ecb141552eb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328639} :answer-field/id #uuid "381407f6-8896-57f4-8153-d40f382fa1ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329294}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "03ce47aa-60a1-561f-9a2d-d11c8a6e24bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-4334" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{36-{x}^{2}}}\\text{d}x\\,=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{36-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{36\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/36)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/36}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/6)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{6}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{6}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=6\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{36-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/6)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (6\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332735 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20636742-aec8-533d-81ab-483f87790c99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(4x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330228} {:answer/id #uuid "38566a19-7854-56cf-af3a-e54d537a1d3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330453} {:answer/id #uuid "526ca6ab-aa62-5847-a02f-822078fec297" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(4x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330700} {:answer/id #uuid "574c08c3-be86-5c8a-8004-c16318247a1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330731} {:answer/id #uuid "a94c081b-466b-5fb0-a0ba-fcb864725ee9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(4x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a94c081b-466b-5fb0-a0ba-fcb864725ee9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(4x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331452} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8b5e79f-94df-55e7-982d-e299729c78cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332551}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0234d108-fb03-514f-bf51-2014068d6893" :question/math-academy-id "q-49535" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $16{x}^{2}=(4x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=4x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(4x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(4x)}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342064 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2383613a-52a1-5d64-8c26-ecd04de30f0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339435} {:answer/id #uuid "4c648079-c85a-5f5e-8976-d0479a4da8f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339821} {:answer/id #uuid "6b5550ab-a530-5982-a558-83f8aec51f26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340078} {:answer/id #uuid "7c200317-7a2d-5a1a-9a82-89183fc7851c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340244} {:answer/id #uuid "ec37b5d7-c2b9-52a3-ad41-1f64c1e8cd40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec37b5d7-c2b9-52a3-ad41-1f64c1e8cd40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341210} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba24916a-286f-51a8-ad99-99bcf753abe6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341703}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "279b83c3-9e48-526a-b453-9a5fa23b12aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-73712" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{8}{3\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:   \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8}{3\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{8}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/4)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)}^{2}.$ \n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{2}.$ Differentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=2\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8}{3\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{4}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (2\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186580893 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c31c8f6-d9d8-53c5-b2d5-4515c416102e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580428} {:answer/id #uuid "5de5a8c0-40fe-5080-8dcd-16fa4bea9378" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580544} {:answer/id #uuid "8c9a5de0-f659-5f3b-acd0-b7b08a36484f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580628} {:answer/id #uuid "d0c414a5-ad71-5780-8d90-e3844295abee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(4x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580715} {:answer/id #uuid "ec6e8ea5-4e2c-5195-ac1d-c3213d882366" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5de5a8c0-40fe-5080-8dcd-16fa4bea9378" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580544} :answer-field/id #uuid "75e64c80-fb76-53ed-a478-ee475bda1a6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580834}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "26a6ef81-4a35-59c2-9081-35e0aed550d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-49545" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16-{x}^{2}}}\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/16)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/16}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/4)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{4}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=4\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16-{x}^{2}}}\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{(x/4)}^{2}}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (4\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676536 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c498ea9-5b57-5d02-ba93-e5238f5e175b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(5 x \\right)}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676552} {:answer/id #uuid "51e6a567-15e0-5bb3-9346-244f71b4e83a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(5 x \\right)}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676583} {:answer/id #uuid "73afaad6-3cc0-5ad1-b38f-24a51fbfb172" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(x \\right)}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676605} {:answer/id #uuid "a82aab25-2af8-5c79-9225-5a8532b62969" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(5 x \\right)}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676638} {:answer/id #uuid "c7e001ab-cad0-5388-aeb9-ba256ce34f46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(5 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c498ea9-5b57-5d02-ba93-e5238f5e175b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(5 x \\right)}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676552} :answer-field/id #uuid "28988c58-40b0-5576-90c1-baecb434fc34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676557}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "00c0df7b-f3f7-5aef-8a44-20715d50042d" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\frac{1}{5}}{\\sqrt{1 - 25 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Use the linear substitution $u=5 x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=5,\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\frac{1}{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{\\frac{1}{5}}{\\sqrt{1 - 25 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{1}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(5 x)^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{1}{5}(\\frac{1}{5})\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{1}{25}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}}{25}+C \\\\  &= \\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(5 x \\right)}}{25}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676540 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/