lty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1d205cfc-223d-5f12-94e3-54557487a6df" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{4}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}=4\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{4})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=4\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4=2$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=2\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the supplied primitive:\n\n$$\n2\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=2\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n2\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{4} \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679747 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2905b413-bec8-5457-a9ab-da7f8c1307bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{4 x}{5} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679751} {:answer/id #uuid "45d77756-bddb-512e-9a28-12964b46ae37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{8 x}{5} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679770} {:answer/id #uuid "8462dca9-837c-583e-ab33-49c85dc0a377" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{8 x}{5} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679816} {:answer/id #uuid "ce1ef3f3-0241-5334-9309-241a050c9cc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{4 x}{5} \\