/ref 17592186679745}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7ae327cb-d047-56a3-9c96-709a008c4721" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{9 - 4 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{2 x}{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{2}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{9 - 4 x^{2}}=3\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{2 x}{3})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $1\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}=\\frac{3}{2}$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{9 - 4 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the supplied primitive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{2 x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679810 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e7cfa1e-0fcf-5c6f-a38b-58c8d91d433e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679792} {:answer/id #uuid "72281e4d-d8e3-5aa3-806e-897099cb473b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679796} {:answer/id #uuid "cbdddafa-9be7-5e98-973b-dd4f3bb7695d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592